    "### cross_val_score()\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose**: Evaluate a score by cross-validation, providing a more reliable performance estimate.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Syntax**: `cross_val_score(estimator, X, y, cv=5, scoring='accuracy')`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Parameters**:\n",
    "- `estimator`: The model to evaluate (e.g., KNeighborsClassifier)\n",
    "- `X`: Feature dataset\n",
    "- `y`: Target variable\n",
    "- `cv`: Number of folds (e.g., 5 or 10)\n",
    "- `scoring`: Evaluation metric (e.g., 'accuracy', 'f1')\n",
    "\n",
    "**Return value**: Array of scores, one for each fold\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why it is appropriate here**: Cross-validation provides a more reliable performance estimate than a single train-test split by averaging across multiple splits, reducing the impact of any particular data partition."
   ]
