  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### precision_score()\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose**: Calculate precision (positive predictive value).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Syntax**: `precision_score(y_true, y_pred)`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Parameters**:\n",
    "- `y_true`: True labels\n",
    "- `y_pred`: Predicted labels\n",
    "\n",
    "**Return value**: Precision score (0.0 to 1.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why it is appropriate here**: Precision measures how many predicted malignancies are actually malignant. In medical contexts, high precision means fewer false positives (fewer healthy patients incorrectly flagged as having cancer)."
