    "### recall_score()\n",
    "\n",
    "**Purpose**: Calculate recall (sensitivity, true positive rate).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Syntax**: `recall_score(y_true, y_pred)`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Parameters**:\n",
    "- `y_true`: True labels\n",
    "- `y_pred`: Predicted labels\n",
    "\n",
    "**Return value**: Recall score (0.0 to 1.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why it is appropriate here**: Recall measures how many actual malignancies are correctly identified. In medical contexts, high recall is critical because missing a malignant tumor (false negative) is far more dangerous than a false positive."
